<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sappi says Saiccor strike resolved.</title>
<headline>Sappi says Saiccor strike resolved.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African paper and pulp group Sappi Ltd said on Tuesday a pay strike at its Saiccor mill in KwaZulu-Natal province had been resolved and workers had returned to their posts.</p>
<p>A statement said agreement was reached on Monday with the Pulp, Paper, Wood and Allied Workers Union on a 7.0 percent across the board wage increase.</p>
<p>It said mill output had been maintained at a level sufficient to meet customer needs despite the strike.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +2711 482-1003</p>
</text>
